                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f69c97ed-9157-4f8f-b61e-e65b73c106f3",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0fd1608-9236-3bad-a6f9-b56084a1e8c6",
                        "source_sense_id": "4b361b8e-9540-3a2b-bed2-e735098c9998",
                        "source_sense_description": "kleines Körnchen, Partikel",
                        "target_lang_word": "toz parçacığı",
                        "target_lang_code": "tr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ed6ff002-4e8c-408b-916b-c7f0a0b3d5ae",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0fd1608-9236-3bad-a6f9-b56084a1e8c6",
                        "source_sense_id": "ba0aea47-deb5-3371-99d4-74419074458a",
                        "source_sense_description": "einzelnes Staubkorn/Staubteilchen",
                        "target_lang_word": "atomy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "atomy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8af7cc51-e4cf-36a4-b392-d980b4bc506f",
                                        "entry_id": "dd62db25-c6ee-37ae-95c8-386e82b7c7b4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A floating mote or speck of dust."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "548c5e59-243d-45d9-893e-01b86244fb9b",
                                                "sense_id": "8af7cc51-e4cf-36a4-b392-d980b4bc506f",
                                                "text": "And thicker then in sunne are Atomies,\nFlew bullets, fier, and slaughtered dead mens cries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5141033-c49c-419c-87b1-82210661569c",
                                                "sense_id": "8af7cc51-e4cf-36a4-b392-d980b4bc506f",
                                                "text": "That eyes, that are the frail’st and softest things\nWho shut their coward gates on atomies\nShould be call’d tyrants, butchers, murderers!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d94471a-8175-4e3c-9c0e-280a45361a2e",
                                                "sense_id": "8af7cc51-e4cf-36a4-b392-d980b4bc506f",
                                                "text": "Thinke not that all betwixt the Wherpoole, and the Sprat,\nI goe about to name, that were to take in hand,\nThe Atomy to tell, or to cast vp the sand;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a56f912-1a69-4742-8f8b-e96d0246527b",
                                                "sense_id": "8af7cc51-e4cf-36a4-b392-d980b4bc506f",
                                                "text": "[…] the crew\nSeemed in that light, like atomies to dance\nWithin a sunbeam;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0335ef64-98e6-40c3-a010-3b50b1feb864",
                                                "sense_id": "8af7cc51-e4cf-36a4-b392-d980b4bc506f",
                                                "text": "1880, Richard Francis Burton, The Kasidah, London: H. S. Nichols, 1894, p. 7,\nThe marvel is that man can smile dreaming his ghostly ghastly dream;—\nBetter the heedless atomy that buzzes in the morning beam!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29ebf343-f7e4-3c49-809e-6ead894de60c",
                                        "entry_id": "dd62db25-c6ee-37ae-95c8-386e82b7c7b4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An indivisible particle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4a4937d-ea0e-41b0-a613-f25b1a7a783d",
                                                "sense_id": "29ebf343-f7e4-3c49-809e-6ead894de60c",
                                                "text": "Lastly, it [an Element] is the least part or Atomie of that thing which is made, or proceedeth from it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fe26a45-ab11-4e4d-be73-b4480bc8d593",
                                                "sense_id": "29ebf343-f7e4-3c49-809e-6ead894de60c",
                                                "text": "And freely men confesse that this world’s spent,\nWhen in the Planets, and the firmament\nThey seeke so many new; they see that this\nIs crumbled out againe to his Atomies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6493403c-ea29-4c14-8b77-3a5815a1840b",
                                                "sense_id": "29ebf343-f7e4-3c49-809e-6ead894de60c",
                                                "text": "[…] praise thy God,\nO be not selfe-conceited, least his rod\nDoe bruise thee into Atomies;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a4051275-a41f-3880-be57-1b171328cb43",
                                        "entry_id": "dd62db25-c6ee-37ae-95c8-386e82b7c7b4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tiny being; a very small person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a46956a2-b123-4eb3-a66e-5303e90cd711",
                                                "sense_id": "a4051275-a41f-3880-be57-1b171328cb43",
                                                "text": "[…] she [Queen Mab] comes\nIn shape no bigger than an agate-stone\nOn the fore-finger of an alderman,\nDrawn with a team of little atomies\nAthwart men’s noses as they lie asleep;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "955f5573-4c15-4930-afeb-9fff5ece5584",
                                                "sense_id": "a4051275-a41f-3880-be57-1b171328cb43",
                                                "text": "Was there a \"delicate atomy\" of minute dimensions and pale complexion, he forthwith strutted a hardy Highlander."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7cbf0031-7067-4a17-9582-d23d061d30c1",
                                                "sense_id": "a4051275-a41f-3880-be57-1b171328cb43",
                                                "text": "“Hey!” he said, “why, it’s Tom! I suppose you have come here to laugh at me, you spiteful little atomy?”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "atomy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7460960-3848-3d02-8cd5-b5507e28a4e7",
                                        "entry_id": "0a7a9f8b-2442-3195-b85f-06d0c18f63fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A skeleton."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34abb22e-f2a8-42f6-ad54-df77e8d50700",
                                                "sense_id": "a7460960-3848-3d02-8cd5-b5507e28a4e7",
                                                "text": "Hostess Quickly. Ay, come, you starv’d bloodhound.\nDoll Tearsheet. Goodman death, goodman bones!\nHostess Quickly. Thou atomy, thou!\nDoll Tearsheet. Come, you thin thing! come, you rascal!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "decf51c6-04f8-45b5-854a-4d743f538c20",
                                                "sense_id": "a7460960-3848-3d02-8cd5-b5507e28a4e7",
                                                "text": "1728, John Gay, The Beggar’s Opera, Dublin: George Risk et al., Act II, Scene 1, p. 67,\nI could not save him from those fleaing Rascals the Surgeons; and now, poor Man, he is among the Otamys [sic] at Surgeon's Hall."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5123a23-3eea-4df2-908c-d4c11b440ab3",
                                                "sense_id": "a7460960-3848-3d02-8cd5-b5507e28a4e7",
                                                "text": "I was now thrown into a violent perturbation of spirit; for I never could behold an atomy without fear and trembling, even when I knew it was no more than a composition of dry bones;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "746fb8fd-fd63-4fae-854d-714a9d02f49c",
                                                "sense_id": "a7460960-3848-3d02-8cd5-b5507e28a4e7",
                                                "text": "[…] a bedstead with four bare atomies of posts, each terminating in a spike, as if for the dismal accommodation of lodgers who might prefer to impale themselves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1522c8be-a9ae-4caa-acea-5ce0f3960ff8",
                                                "sense_id": "a7460960-3848-3d02-8cd5-b5507e28a4e7",
                                                "text": "The veriest atomy he looked,\nWith grimy fingers clutching and crooked,\nTight skin, a nose all bony and hooked,\nAnd a shaking, sharp, suspicious way;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "atomy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb7c6709-5c3c-33f8-ae1e-85c411998efd",
                                        "entry_id": "8a213208-4be1-3a30-a33e-87d1673ee228",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Resembling a tiny particle; made up of tiny particles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d126ba7-b2ed-4510-b90b-50213ca4ffcb",
                                                "sense_id": "bb7c6709-5c3c-33f8-ae1e-85c411998efd",
                                                "text": "[…] noble Lesser Alps which were clothed in rich velvety green all the way up and had little atomy Swiss homes perched upon grassy benches along their mist-dimmed heights."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24a21b1b-67f4-45d2-9e16-40080ef2d04c",
                                                "sense_id": "bb7c6709-5c3c-33f8-ae1e-85c411998efd",
                                                "text": "1894, Richard Henry Savage, The Princess of Alaska, Chicago and New York: Rand, McNally, Book 2, Chapter 8, p. 235,\n[…] the atomy speck, hurled through space, which we mortals call the world!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a91fb4e9-6531-4c1a-91a2-cba95f27b575",
                                                "sense_id": "bb7c6709-5c3c-33f8-ae1e-85c411998efd",
                                                "text": "Things that flit in the sky or creep\nIn the atomy dust, or swarm in the deep,"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0ffa81f4-753a-4715-aed6-ce8f4067b3cb",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0fd1608-9236-3bad-a6f9-b56084a1e8c6",
                        "source_sense_id": "ba0aea47-deb5-3371-99d4-74419074458a",
                        "source_sense_description": "einzelnes Staubkorn/Staubteilchen",
                        "target_lang_word": "mote",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mote",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "92031fef-3674-3d4d-8790-326a53fe23aa",
                                        "entry_id": "575746a7-4150-3208-b541-5547b54d3488",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small particle; a speck."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8684a2df-3272-4c82-b2e9-6cef2d7bd638",
                                                "sense_id": "92031fef-3674-3d4d-8790-326a53fe23aa",
                                                "text": "Thou hypocrite, first cast out the beam out of thine own eye; and then shalt thou see clearly to cast out the mote out of thy brother’s eye."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ca63389-b1f3-4cd0-af39-50f0f92d42bb",
                                                "sense_id": "92031fef-3674-3d4d-8790-326a53fe23aa",
                                                "text": "What shall a Mote up to a Monarch rise?\nAn Emmet match an Emperor in might?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df75e927-8a8e-4078-b428-7a91815874ba",
                                                "sense_id": "92031fef-3674-3d4d-8790-326a53fe23aa",
                                                "text": "I wanted to shrink myself to a mote of dust, plunge into this pool I held in my own cyclopean hands, soar down these runs of light to places where light itself was born from this colloquy of dust."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mote",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6dd5647a-eafb-3861-815c-9ab9b59e62fb",
                                        "entry_id": "ee1a6481-f79b-3d8f-bf9b-117b9cb41519",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "May or might."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "no-present-participle"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f95d8199-c327-4d53-a2ee-8d5b620064e3",
                                                "sense_id": "6dd5647a-eafb-3861-815c-9ab9b59e62fb",
                                                "text": "he […] kept aloofe for dread to be descryde, / Untill fit time and place he mote espy, / Where he mote worke him scath and villeny."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac7daa21-f938-3963-8663-80de3a8966a7",
                                        "entry_id": "ee1a6481-f79b-3d8f-bf9b-117b9cb41519",
                                        "glosses": [
